# Browser verification

Check web UI in a headless browser against the local dev server. Do not use macOS Screen Recording or Cursor Computer Use.

## Do

- Start `bun run dev` in `dev/memli` when it is not already running (Vite at `http://localhost:5173`).
- Launch headless Brave with its own profile and a DevTools port, then drive the page over the Chrome DevTools Protocol: navigate, wait for rendered text, click, and read `location` plus `innerText`.

```bash
"/Applications/Brave Browser.app/Contents/MacOS/Brave Browser" \
  --headless=new --disable-gpu \
  --user-data-dir=/tmp/memli-brave-verify \
  --remote-debugging-port=9222 \
  about:blank
```

- Confirm the behavior the change is supposed to produce. Stop the headless browser when the check is done.

## Do not

- Call Computer Use (`computer_screenshot`, `computer_click`, `computer_start_control`, or any screen-scope action).
- Ask the user to turn on Screen Recording or Accessibility for verification.
- Treat `curl` or `--dump-dom` as proof. Vite's `#root` is empty until JavaScript runs.
